## Why This Is Asked
Tests breadth of AWS data platform design: multi-region, batch/streaming, cataloging, governance, and testability.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region landing, streaming to Parquet, Glue ETL, Glue Data Catalog
- Lake Formation cross-region access, idempotent ingestions, schema evolution
- Lightweight data quality checks and end-to-end test harness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: idempotent ingest
const seen = new Set();
function ingest(record){
  if(seen.has(record.ingest_id)) return;
  seen.add(record.ingest_id);
  // transform and persist
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement drift detection with Glue Schema Registry and monitoring?
- How do you validate cross-region access policies at scale?
